WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:02.467
-Welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:04.133
Thank you so much for coming.
-Thanks, man.

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:06.234
-Thanks for having me.
-How is the fam?

00:00:06.234 --> 00:00:08.033
I was very lucky to meet

00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:10.801
your beautiful daughter
backstage.

00:00:10.801 --> 00:00:12.267
Frankie.
-Frankie came with me, yeah.

00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:13.634
-She's a good kid.

00:00:13.634 --> 00:00:15.300
-She's a great kid.

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:20.200
You know, most of the time,
she's a great kid.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:24.067
She's 14, you know, so, like,

00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:26.033
I'm here in New York
because I'm working.

00:00:26.033 --> 00:00:28.200
I'm shooting season two
of "Severance."

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:32.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:34.334
But my family lives
in Los Angeles

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:39.033
so we spend a ton of time
on Face Time, you know,

00:00:39.033 --> 00:00:42.067
like, constantly,
because it's terrible being

00:00:42.067 --> 00:00:44.934
on opposite sides
of the country -- it's hard.

00:00:44.934 --> 00:00:47.567
So we're always talking
Face Time.

00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:50.100
But my daughter, Frankie,
who you just met,

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:54.434
she is constantly
taking screenshots

00:00:54.434 --> 00:00:58.033
of me -- of, like, my face.

00:00:58.033 --> 00:00:59.534
Because when you're doing
Face Time,

00:00:59.534 --> 00:01:02.334
it's not like you're on,
like, a fancy Zoom

00:01:02.334 --> 00:01:03.334
and you have a ring light,

00:01:03.334 --> 00:01:04.801
and you, like, primp yourself.

00:01:04.801 --> 00:01:08.167
You're, like, getting ready
for bed or eating or whatever.

00:01:08.167 --> 00:01:10.534
-Yeah, it's family time, yeah.
-It's family time.

00:01:10.534 --> 00:01:14.701
And she -- every single time
I see that flash

00:01:14.701 --> 00:01:18.334
on the screen, it's just like,
"Jesus, really?"

00:01:18.334 --> 00:01:22.868
And so this past year,
they made a calendar

00:01:22.868 --> 00:01:24.133
of all of those photos.

00:01:24.133 --> 00:01:25.701
They collected them

00:01:25.701 --> 00:01:27.734
and made a calendar.

00:01:27.734 --> 00:01:29.467
-Of unflattering photos of you.

00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:31.701
-Yes.
-You brought a few here.

00:01:31.701 --> 00:01:33.868
I just want to show them on
national TV, if you don't mind.

00:01:33.868 --> 00:01:35.133
-Yeah, that'd be great.

00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:36.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:36.601 --> 00:01:38.801
That'd be great.

00:01:38.801 --> 00:01:41.601
-This here is some of the
screenshots right here.

00:01:41.601 --> 00:01:42.701
-Yeah.

00:01:42.701 --> 00:01:46.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:50.000
-Nice, nice.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.467
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.467 --> 00:01:52.534
-What a great family.

00:01:52.534 --> 00:01:55.634
-Yeah, it's nice.
-What a lovely family.

00:01:55.634 --> 00:01:57.234
-You know --

00:01:57.234 --> 00:01:59.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:59.367 --> 00:02:01.367
I feel like everyone

00:02:01.367 --> 00:02:03.801
looks great when
they're blowing their nose.

00:02:03.801 --> 00:02:06.067
-[ Laughs ] Everyone does.
-Yeah.

00:02:06.067 --> 00:02:07.467
-You mentioned that you're here
filming season two

00:02:07.467 --> 00:02:08.667
of "Severance."

00:02:08.667 --> 00:02:11.434
Congratulations.
Season one was such a huge hit.

00:02:11.434 --> 00:02:13.100
I loved it.
You've been nominated

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:16.467
for almost every award there is.

00:02:16.467 --> 00:02:17.701
Congratulations.
Golden Globes, everything.

00:02:17.701 --> 00:02:18.701
-Thank you.

00:02:18.701 --> 00:02:19.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:19.901 --> 00:02:23.133
-Emmys -- What can you tell us
about season two?

00:02:23.133 --> 00:02:24.200
-You know,
that's the funny thing

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:27.133
is when we're making season one,

00:02:27.133 --> 00:02:30.534
we were like,
"This is so weird,

00:02:30.534 --> 00:02:32.334
like, is anyone gonna like this

00:02:32.334 --> 00:02:34.634
or is everyone just gonna
think this is stupid?"

00:02:34.634 --> 00:02:36.868
Like, we couldn't tell.

00:02:36.868 --> 00:02:40.033
We loved it and everything,
but you never know.

00:02:40.033 --> 00:02:43.367
And it just seemed so strange
that we didn't know.

00:02:43.367 --> 00:02:46.634
And now, like,
we have to -- like, all this --

00:02:46.634 --> 00:02:49.667
We have secret scripts and have
to use, like, code words

00:02:49.667 --> 00:02:52.901
when we're on e-mail and, like,
it's so secret.

00:02:52.901 --> 00:02:54.434
It's crazy.

00:02:54.434 --> 00:02:56.801
And it's just feels ridiculous.

00:02:56.801 --> 00:02:59.834
But it's also great,
because people want to know,

00:02:59.834 --> 00:03:01.367
you know.
-Could we set up

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:02.968
the first season of "Severance"

00:03:02.968 --> 00:03:04.767
or just what "Severance" is
if you haven't seen the show?

00:03:04.767 --> 00:03:07.734
-Yeah, sure, it's a show
that takes place in a world

00:03:07.734 --> 00:03:11.167
where there's a technology where
you can split your life in half.

00:03:11.167 --> 00:03:12.667
So when you go to work,

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:14.868
you don't know who you are
in the outside world.

00:03:14.868 --> 00:03:17.701
And then when you're at home,
you have no idea

00:03:17.701 --> 00:03:19.334
who you are at work
or what your job is

00:03:19.334 --> 00:03:20.834
or what you do there.

00:03:20.834 --> 00:03:24.567
So it's essentially two
separate lives you're leading.

00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:27.000
-Yeah, that's a great way
to set it up and then watch it,

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.567
and it just gets crazier
and crazier.

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:30.567
It's fantastic.
-Oh, thanks, man.

00:03:30.567 --> 00:03:32.300
-I'm just so excited
that you're here

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:34.334
and that you're here
during a very important time.

00:03:34.334 --> 00:03:36.501
It's Perm Week
on "The Tonight Show."

00:03:36.501 --> 00:03:38.567
And it's a --
-You know, Chris

00:03:38.567 --> 00:03:40.701
has a wonderful head of hair,

00:03:40.701 --> 00:03:42.267
and you made it even better.
-Right, yeah.

00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:43.767
-Like, incredible.

00:03:43.767 --> 00:03:45.567
-His hair in general was,
like, unbelievable.

00:03:45.567 --> 00:03:46.734
-Yeah.
-I wouldn't even touch it.

00:03:46.734 --> 00:03:49.067
I would frame his hair.
-Yeah.

00:03:49.067 --> 00:03:50.834
-And then he did it, and now
it even looks even better.

00:03:50.834 --> 00:03:52.133
-Oh, it's beautiful.
-It's beautiful.

00:03:52.133 --> 00:03:53.667
Have you ever done a perm,
or thought about it?

00:03:53.667 --> 00:03:56.501
-Oh, I really -- I mean,
in the '80s, it seemed like

00:03:56.501 --> 00:03:59.767
men were getting -- like, guys
that hosted, like,

00:03:59.767 --> 00:04:01.534
afternoon talk shows had perms.

00:04:01.534 --> 00:04:03.400
-Everybody, yeah, of course,
yeah, I remember.

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:06.334
-Gary Collins would have a perm.
-He did have one, yeah.

00:04:06.334 --> 00:04:08.534
-Adam Curry, I think, right?
-Oh, yeah, yeah, yeah, sure,

00:04:08.534 --> 00:04:09.601
Adam Curry, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:04:09.601 --> 00:04:11.567
I found a old headshot of you,

00:04:11.567 --> 00:04:13.734
not permed, just kind of cool,
I would say.

00:04:13.734 --> 00:04:16.801
-This is my first headshot,
I believe.

00:04:16.801 --> 00:04:18.901
-This feels '90s, right?
-It's '90s.

00:04:18.901 --> 00:04:21.467
It's like -- Oh, my God.

00:04:21.467 --> 00:04:23.567
You know, listen...

00:04:23.567 --> 00:04:24.567
-Who do you --
Wow, you look good.

00:04:24.567 --> 00:04:25.634
-It's like --

00:04:25.634 --> 00:04:28.634
[ Cheers and applause ]
Don't clap.

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:29.968
You can't clap.

00:04:29.968 --> 00:04:32.434
My hair is like a cross
between, like, Eddie Vedder

00:04:32.434 --> 00:04:35.133
and Natalie Merchant.
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:35.133 --> 00:04:36.167
I like your pose.

00:04:36.167 --> 00:04:37.300
How did you --
How does one even --

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:38.334
Look at -- no, look at --

00:04:38.334 --> 00:04:40.234
-Oh, my God. It's so terrible.

00:04:40.234 --> 00:04:41.968
It's so --
-That looks difficult.

00:04:41.968 --> 00:04:47.033
-I mean, that is, like,
profoundly bad.

00:04:47.033 --> 00:04:49.067
Like, that's really tough.

00:04:49.067 --> 00:04:50.334
-I love it.

00:04:50.334 --> 00:04:53.734
I just didn't want you
to feel left out...

00:04:53.734 --> 00:04:55.033
-Yeah, I'm sure.
-...so I --

00:04:55.033 --> 00:04:56.400
-Oh, yeah.

00:04:56.400 --> 00:04:57.501
-Would you?
-Please!

00:04:57.501 --> 00:04:59.467
-Can I, please?
-Yeah, please, just...

00:04:59.467 --> 00:05:03.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:03.667 --> 00:05:08.000
♪♪

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:12.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:12.634 --> 00:05:14.033
-I love it.
-It feels good.

00:05:14.033 --> 00:05:16.067
-I love it.
-It feels right.

00:05:16.067 --> 00:05:19.467
-Oh, it's so...
-It feels -- This feels right.

00:05:19.467 --> 00:05:21.634
-I feel like my life
coming together.

00:05:21.634 --> 00:05:23.133
-Yeah, this is it.

00:05:23.133 --> 00:05:24.534
See, you're getting
what Chris was feeling earlier.

00:05:24.534 --> 00:05:25.601
-Yes.
-And you're getting

00:05:25.601 --> 00:05:26.801
a little taste of it now.
-That's right.

00:05:26.801 --> 00:05:29.067
-This is --
Can we talk about "Party Down"?

00:05:29.067 --> 00:05:30.367
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Please.

00:05:30.367 --> 00:05:32.033
This has been -- I missed this.

00:05:32.033 --> 00:05:33.434
This has been --
-Yeah.

00:05:33.434 --> 00:05:36.133
We're just gonna leave the wigs.
-Yeah, I'm not taking these off.

00:05:36.133 --> 00:05:37.701
-13 years...

00:05:37.701 --> 00:05:41.367
-13 years since we got canceled
in 2010.

00:05:41.367 --> 00:05:45.801
-But what would you --
what was it?

00:05:45.801 --> 00:05:48.133
It was just streaming
that made it popular again?

00:05:48.133 --> 00:05:50.767
-I guess so.
Because when we finished,

00:05:50.767 --> 00:05:53.300
when we were canceled, we were
canceled for, like,

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:55.567
pretty good reason, I guess.

00:05:55.567 --> 00:05:59.133
Because our our ratings
were literally 0.0.

00:05:59.133 --> 00:06:01.133
-No one was watching.
-No.

00:06:01.133 --> 00:06:03.200
-No one watching your show?
-No.

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:05.300
So you end up getting canceled.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:07.167
-That's what happens
when no one watches your show.

00:06:07.167 --> 00:06:11.334
-But little by little over
the years, people got into it.

00:06:11.334 --> 00:06:14.701
And now I get asked about it,
just, like, out on the street

00:06:14.701 --> 00:06:16.000
or whatever.
-Well, it's a cult favorite.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:17.067
-We get asked about it just
as much as anything else.

00:06:17.067 --> 00:06:18.267
-Really?
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:06:18.267 --> 00:06:19.767
It's great.
-But everyone came back for it.

00:06:19.767 --> 00:06:21.167
-Yeah, yeah.

00:06:21.167 --> 00:06:23.767
Lizzy Caplan, because of
scheduling, couldn't do it.

00:06:23.767 --> 00:06:26.501
But everyone else --
Jane Lynch, Ken Marino,

00:06:26.501 --> 00:06:29.434
Megan Mullally, Ryan Hansen,
Martin Starr, everybody.

00:06:29.434 --> 00:06:31.100
-But then who --
and Jennifer Garner --

00:06:31.100 --> 00:06:33.000
-Jennifer Garner joined
the show.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:34.033
-I love Jennifer Garner.
-Yeah.

00:06:34.033 --> 00:06:35.033
-Come on.
-She's amazing.

00:06:35.033 --> 00:06:36.501
-I can't get enough
Jennifer Garner.

00:06:36.501 --> 00:06:38.067
I love her.
-She's the best.

00:06:38.067 --> 00:06:40.133
-Do we set this up at all?
How do we set up --

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:42.267
-Yeah, this is, I believe Roman,
Martin Starr's character,

00:06:42.267 --> 00:06:45.567
and I talking
in the first episode.

00:06:45.567 --> 00:06:46.634
-There you go.

00:06:46.634 --> 00:06:49.434
-I don't have
a perm in this clip.

00:06:49.434 --> 00:06:51.701
-Don't let everyone down.
-Sorry.

00:06:51.701 --> 00:06:54.567
-Guys, no booing when you watch
this clip.

00:06:54.567 --> 00:06:55.901
Enjoy it, it's a comedy.

00:06:55.901 --> 00:06:58.200
Oh, we should mention
that it's a catering company.

00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:02.501
-Yeah, "Party Down" is about
a catering company.

00:07:02.501 --> 00:07:04.734
-Thank you.
-A non-permed catering company.

00:07:04.734 --> 00:07:07.200
That's all you need to know.
-Why would -- yeah.

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:09.267
It is --
I'm so happy it's back.

00:07:09.267 --> 00:07:10.601
I want to show everybody a clip.

00:07:10.601 --> 00:07:12.567
Here's Adam Scott in
the new season of "Party Down."

00:07:12.567 --> 00:07:13.767
Take a look.

00:07:13.767 --> 00:07:17.234
-I accept the possibility
that I probably won't be

00:07:17.234 --> 00:07:18.767
appreciated in my lifetime.

00:07:18.767 --> 00:07:21.467
You know, if I get discovered
as they're reviewing my papers

00:07:21.467 --> 00:07:24.200
after I die,
well, I'll be fine with that.

00:07:24.200 --> 00:07:26.534
-So you still doing
mostly hard sci-fi?

00:07:26.534 --> 00:07:28.300
-Yeah. You remember
the magnum opus

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:30.300
that I started
on a roll of toilet paper?

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:31.601
Well, that was
just the beginning,

00:07:31.601 --> 00:07:33.634
and I'm just kind of
tweaking one little thing,

00:07:33.634 --> 00:07:35.367
but then it's ready to sell.

00:07:35.367 --> 00:07:37.901
And I still have my blog,
which is now a vlog

00:07:37.901 --> 00:07:39.267
because of my carpal tunnel
incident.

00:07:39.267 --> 00:07:40.467
-You know what?

00:07:40.467 --> 00:07:42.968
I should probably go on out
to the dinner.

00:07:42.968 --> 00:07:44.968
-Yeah, see you in 12 years.

00:07:44.968 --> 00:07:46.801
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:46.801 --> 00:07:48.000
[ Cheers and applause ]
-It's so good, man.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:49.634
-Thanks, man.
-It made me laugh.

00:07:49.634 --> 00:07:51.000
And I've seen
the great reviews, as well.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:52.067
-Thanks, dude.
-It's getting great reviews.

00:07:52.067 --> 00:07:53.400
-Thank you.
-Adam Scott, everybody.

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:56.767
"Party Down" premieres
its third season next Friday

00:07:56.767 --> 00:07:58.300
on Starz.

00:07:58.300 --> 00:08:01.033
Frankie, keep it up.
That's a good job.

00:08:01.033 --> 00:08:02.200
We'll be right back
with more "Tonight Show",

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:03.467
everybody.
Good job, Frankie.

00:08:03.467 --> 00:08:04.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

